# ⭑ BUILD OUTPUT IS NOT SOURCE (Josh, 2026-09-09). `build/` was tracked, so
#   every local build dirtied the tree, `git add -A` was a hazard, and the
#   release workflow actually FAILED on it: the DSP is cross-compiled in Docker
#   as root, so build/obj came back root-owned and `git checkout` could not
#   unlink it — after the release had already been published.
#   Untracking keeps the files on disk; it only stops git carrying them.
build/
tools/__pycache__/
